@startuml uc003-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-003 Execute target model: analysis sequence (main success scenario)

control "Execute Target" as Exec
entity "Benchmark" as B
boundary "Target Model Interface" as TMI
entity "Target Result" as TR
boundary "Progress Listener" as PLis

[-> Exec : execute(benchmark, target)
Exec -> B : get test cases, in order
B --> Exec : test cases
loop for each test case
  Exec -> TMI : send(question), once
  TMI --> Exec : model response
  Exec -> TR : create(test case, model response)
  Exec -> PLis : case executed(target result)
end
[<-- Exec : target results, in benchmark order

note right of TMI
  2a: a connector error becomes the result's error,
  and the loop goes on.
  2b: an auth or quota error also sets the stop
  reason; later cases are not sent and get the
  error "not sent: run stopped after ...".
  2c: anything else is a bug and escapes.
  3a: a refusal or cut-off answer is still
  a model response.
end note
@enduml
